issue.description:
Refine the Design system → Colors preview typography hierarchy so semantic group headings become stronger visual anchors while token labels return to normal title case.

## Overall direction

The current state uses title-case semantic group headings such as Primary / Secondary and uppercase token labels such as BACKGROUND / FOREGROUND.

Change that hierarchy so:

* semantic group headings become uppercase and one typography step larger;
* token labels return to normal title case;
* token labels remain smaller supporting metadata;
* HEX values remain visually secondary.

This is a presentation-only adjustment for the Design system preview.

## 1. Semantic group headings

Update group headings such as:

* Primary
* Secondary
* Accent
* Base
* Card
* Popover
* Muted
* Destructive
* Border / Input / Ring
* Charts
* Sidebar

Requirements:

* render them in uppercase;
* increase their font size by one typography step from the current implementation;
* if the current size is approximately `text-sm`, move to the next appropriate step such as `text-base`;
* keep using the base foreground semantic color token;
* preserve current grouping/order;
* preserve current spacing/layout unless a small adjustment is needed to accommodate the larger text.

Example:

`Primary` → `PRIMARY`

## 2. Token labels

Remove the uppercase treatment from token display labels.

Examples:

* `BACKGROUND` → `Background`
* `FOREGROUND` → `Foreground`
* `PRIMARY BACKGROUND` → `Primary Background`
* `PRIMARY FOREGROUND` → `Primary Foreground`
* `ACCENT BACKGROUND` → `Accent Background`
* `SIDEBAR BORDER` → `Sidebar Border`
* `SIDEBAR RING` → `Sidebar Ring`

Requirements:

* use normal title case;
* keep the existing smaller supporting font size;
* keep using the base foreground semantic color token;
* preserve current placement beneath each swatch;
* preserve current mapping/wording other than casing.

## 3. HEX values

Preserve current HEX value presentation.

Requirements:

* keep current font size;
* keep current muted/secondary visual treatment;
* do not change HEX conversion or live update behavior.

## 4. Intended hierarchy

The visual hierarchy should read:

1. section heading, e.g. Colors;
2. uppercase semantic group heading, e.g. PRIMARY;
3. title-case token label, e.g. Background;
4. muted HEX value.

The semantic group heading should clearly lead the token label.

## 5. Preserve existing Design system behavior

Do not change:

* swatch dimensions;
* swatch colors;
* two-column layout;
* Sidebar display-label mapping;
* token order/grouping;
* Theme v3;
* actual token keys;
* CSS variables;
* sidebar editor labels;
* alias behavior;
* import/export keys;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry.

No new dependency or network behavior.

## 6. Accessibility and responsiveness

* preserve readable contrast in light/dark modes;
* preserve current responsive layout;
* avoid wrapping or clipping from the larger group headings;
* preserve logical reading order.

## Acceptance

* Semantic group headings are uppercase.
* Semantic group headings are one typography step larger than before.
* Semantic group headings continue using the base foreground token.
* Token labels are no longer uppercase.
* Token labels use normal title case.
* Token labels retain their current smaller supporting size and base foreground color.
* HEX values remain unchanged and visually secondary.
* Existing swatches, token mappings, Theme v3, aliases, sidebar editor labels, import/export, persistence, history, Design Command, mutation operations, and registry remain unchanged.
